> 1. What is riding good for?

Some mounts have special powers (like flying) and also, if you are
especially skilled, you get some bonus when you fight mounted.  Knights are
suppose to excel at this.

>
> 2. Why is some armor not automatically identified when put on, and
> some is?! Quite random...

In general, 'obvious effects' are immediately identified.  Like Armor Class
(which is shown on your statistics lines) and levitation (Geez, I started to
float.  Wonder what these boots I just put on...).  Other effects that are
not obvious are in general not immediately identified.  Except that those
armors that don't get immediately identified either has nothing, or
something that's not obvious, and somewhat 'situational' (i.e., only works
against certain types of attack, etcs)

>
> 3. Why are some food rations in your inventory rotten and some isn't?
> Again, quite random. Do food rations rot in your inventory or are some
> rotten before one picks the up?

Mostly it's random.  Imagine you are camping and picking up food on the
ground.  Some are just bound to be bad.  Some are more likely to be bad than
others (Let's say, food is 'cursed', for example or food that just doesn't
sound like it's particularly appetizing).  But in general, when you eat, you
risk some amount of bad things (and good things)

>
> 4. In the status area, my strenght was indicated 18/02. What does this
> mean?

It's from a game that Nethack originally borrowed some system from (read
Advanced Dungeons and Dragons, which Nethack is not).  For some reason, when
they wanted to give some 'super human strength' (i.e., above 18), they
decided to give rating from 18/01% to 18/100%.  I don't know what came over
them to do that, rather than going '19, 20, 21, etcs'.  But it stuck.
Anything 18/xx is higher than 18.

>
> 5. What is the difference between wearing and eating rings?

Practically speaking, if you wear it, you can remove it (as long as the ring
let you), and you only have 2 ring fingers, according to Nethack reality.
So you can't have more than 2 rings going at the same time.  If you eat it,
you digest it.  So it's part of you now.

