> 9. What is this story about "luck" (eg. you were unlucky/very
> unlucky/luck/etc.)?

Well, the game actually has a few 'hidden' statistics (as oppose to the ones
you know, like hit points).  Luck is one of them along with things like
burden, hunger, speed, and so on.  Luck is even more hidden than those other
stats in general because the effects are not usually told to you even in the
generic term (unlike burden and hunger, where you can tell if you are
burdened/unburdened or hungry/not hungry)  There are only a few ways to
actually check your luck status and it's in general magical.  It affects
certain actions you perform.  Not everything, but many.  There are ways to
manipulate your luck value.  You'll sometimes notice obvious signs of your
luck improving.  Keep experimenting and you'll find some...

